0194: one front-camera frame to memory and out as a snap (bluecam_stream=3)

The IFE-lite's RDI0 write master 0 writes the CSID's RAW10 stream (MIPI
packed) to a 2 MiB buffer below 4 GiB, the same place every frame
(camss-vfe-17x.c reset, vfe_wm_start, reg update). The IFE's SMMU
streams in bypass, the camera AXI and CAMNOC clocks on, the IFE-lite
clock at 384 MHz. Sensor exposure 642 lines, analog gain bluecam_gain
(code, default 768 = 4x). After the stream stops: bytes written, line
stride from the extent, a level histogram, then two snaps through
bluesnap_put() (new in sweet_ufs.c; needs bluesnap_on_reboot=1): the raw
Bayer as grey at 820x616 and an RGGB 2x2 colour image at 410x308.

